    (property "Description" "WeAct Studio RP2350A_V10 core board. Pico-form 2x20 THT, 0.7in row spacing, 27 GPIO (GP0-GP22, GP26-GP29), 4 ADC. GP23=KEY, GP24=LED1, GP25=LED2 are onboard only, not on the headers. POWER TOPOLOGY, measured not assumed: VIN (pad 40) is the USB VBUS side and is UPSTREAM; the pin silkscreened 5V (pad 39) is the system node downstream of an ideal-diode FET and feeds the 3V3 800mA regulator. Feeding VIN propagates to 5V with a 20mV drop; feeding 5V is blocked at VIN (0.01V). An external supply therefore goes on pad 39, NOT pad 40, because pad 39 cannot back-feed USB. This is the opposite of Pico VSYS/VBUS naming."
      (at 0 -10.16 0)
